9.3(6)(A) (A) the name of the Person receiving the service;
9.3(6)(B) (B) the date the service was delivered;
9.3(6)(C) (C) the start and end time the service was delivered;
9.3(6)(D) (D) the name of the DHHS service code that was delivered (EPR);
9.3(6)(E) (E) the name of a Staff providing the services; and
9.3(6)(F) (F) a written summary note of substantive service activities consistent with the service description.

10.4(4)(A) (A) the HHS or PPS Staff is willing to deliver ELS;
10.4(4)(B) (B) the Person (or guardian, if applicable) is choosing the HHS or PPS Staff to deliver ELS;
10.4(4)(C) (C) the HHS or PPS Staff has the capacity to deliver ELS; and
10.4(4)(D) (D) it is in the best interest of the Person to receive ELS from the HHS or PPS Staff.

11.3(2)(A) (A) is integrated in the community and supports the Person having access to the community;
11.3(2)(B) (B) is physically accessible for the Person;
11.3(2)(C) (C) optimizes autonomy and independence for the Person in making life choices and enables the Person to have control of their own schedule, including access to food and visitors;
11.3(2)(D) (D) allows the Person to decorate their personal space;
11.3(2)(E) (E) allows the Person to have privacy, dignity, respect;
11.3(2)(F) (F) ensures the Person has freedom from coercion and restraint; and
11.3(2)(G) (G) is selected by the Person after all residential setting options are offered.

11.3(5)(A) (A) the inventory completion date and the Staff's name that completed the inventory;
11.3(5)(B) (B) belongings that have significant value to the Person;
11.3(5)(C) (C) belongings with a purchase value of $50.00 or more;
11.3(5)(D) (D) all new items added as received by the Person that have significant value to the Person or with a purchase value of $50.00 or more; and
11.3(5)(E) (E) discarded items must be removed, including the reason for discard and signature from the Person or their legal guardian.

11.3(10)(A) (A) the name of the Person receiving the service;
11.3(10)(B) (B) the date the service was delivered;
11.3(10)(C) (C) the name of the DHHS service code delivered (HHS);
11.3(10)(D) (D) the name of a Staff providing the service; and
11.3(10)(E) (E) a written daily summary note of substantive service activities consistent with the service code description.

11.3(11)(A) (A) the name of the Person receiving the service;
11.3(11)(B) (B) the date the service was delivered;
11.3(11)(C) (C) the start and end time the service was delivered ;
11.3(11)(D) (D) the name of the DHHS service code delivered (Direct Support for the HHS Staff);
11.3(11)(E) (E) the name of the Staff providing the service; and
11.3(11)(F) (F) a written summary note of substantive service activities consistent with the individual service description.

13.3(3)(A) (A) the name of the Person receiving the service;
13.3(3)(B) (B) the date the service was delivered;
13.3(3)(C) (C) the Person's pick up location and the drop off location;
13.3(3)(D) (D) the Person's pick up time and drop off time for each instance the Person is picked up or dropped off;
13.3(3)(E) (E) the name of the DHHS service code delivered (MTP); and
13.3(3)(F) (F) the name of the Staff providing the service.

14.3(1) (1) the name of the Person receiving the service;
14.3(2) (2) the date the service was delivered;
14.3(3) (3) the name of the DHHS service code delivered (PAC Daily);
14.3(4) (4) the name of the Staff providing the service; and
14.3(5) (5) a written daily summary note of substantive service activities consistent with the service code description.
